.TH SETUP-SYSTEM 1
.SH NAME
setup-system \- configure a Debian workstation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B setup-system
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the Textual interface in an interactive terminal as the desktop user.
Choose Base system or Working environment, preview the selected changes, and
confirm an individual operation. Saving preferences is independent of Apply.
Press F1 for installed documentation and Ctrl-Q to leave at a safe boundary.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/setup-system/base.toml
Base selections. XDG_CONFIG_HOME overrides the configuration directory.
.TP
.I ~/.config/setup-system/workspace.toml
Workspace selections.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/setup-system/docs/
Offline administration, configuration and recovery guides.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The normal-user interface accepts numeric SETUP_SYSTEM_ preferences for path
completion and runner timeouts. See the installed settings_map.md reference
for accepted names, units, defaults and limits.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR su (1),
.BR sudo (8)
